import LeanFlagAlgebras.Core.Compute.Mask3

/-! # Order-7 certificate data: the six-vertex representatives

The 964 tetrahedron-free isomorphism classes on six vertices, as literal
bitmasks in the `triIdx 6` encoding (bit `triIdx 6 a b c` is the
hyperedge `{a, b, c}`), listed in the same order as the
`H_representatives` field of the certificate JSON.

The kernel checks recorded here: the list has 964 entries, is strictly
increasing (hence duplicate-free), and every mask passes the bit-level
tetrahedron-freeness test — so, through `k4FreeMask_iff_mem`, every
listed mask decodes to a model of the tetrahedron-free theory. That the
listed classes are pairwise non-isomorphic and exhaust the six-vertex
classes is the canonicalization sweep of a later slice; nothing below
depends on it. -/

